1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:08,010
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:09,700
How do you do?

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,430
Hello.

4
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:12,500
I'm Ralph Riley.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,110
I'm Richard Stewart, and this is my wife, Marilyn.

6
00:00:15,110 --> 00:00:15,750
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:16,550
Likewise, Mr. Riley.

8
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:21,290
Please, sit down. What can I do for you?

9
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:24,070
We'd like to discuss a mortgage.

10
00:00:24,070 --> 00:00:25,000
For a house.

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,370
Fine. Are you buying a house

12
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:29,270
or are you refinancing your present home?

13
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:31,150
We're planning to buy a house.

14
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:33,470
And we'd like to find out about a mortgage.

15
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:35,410
We are customers of the bank.

16
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:38,380
As a matter of fact, my whole family banks here.

17
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:41,740
I have some questions to ask.

18
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:44,240
Do you own your house or do you rent?

19
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,190
Neither.

20
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:50,250
We live with my parents, Dr. and Mrs. Philip Stewart.

21
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:52,250
And how old are you?

22
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:53,230
I'm twenty-nine.

23
00:00:53,230 --> 00:00:55,700
I'm thirty.

24
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:58,510
And, Mr. Stewart, what is your occupation?

25
00:00:58,510 --> 00:01:00,370
I'm a freelance photographer.

26
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:01,900
And, Mrs. Stewart, are you working?

27
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:05,370
Yes. I'm a designer, and I work in a boutique.

28
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:07,950
Did you bring any savings or salary information?

29
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:09,200
Last year's tax forms?

30
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:17,280
Yes. Here they are.

31
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,970
OK. What ... what kind of house did you have in mind?

32
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:21,090
We're talking about buying

33
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:23,370
a two-bedroom house in Mount Kisco.

34
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:29,480
Here are the financial details on the house.

35
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,410
Thank you.

36
00:01:30,410 --> 00:01:31,920
Are you prepared to make a ten-percent down payment?

37
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,690
Yes, we are.

38
00:01:33,690 --> 00:01:35,510
Payments over thirty years?

39
00:01:35,510 --> 00:01:39,370
Yes.

40
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:41,800
Do you think we can get a loan?

41
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:46,340
Well, it depends. Do you own any other property?

42
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:49,450
Any stocks or bonds?

43
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:51,550
No.

44
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:56,210
I see. Then you don't have any collateral.

45
00:01:56,210 --> 00:01:58,530
Perhaps you could get a guarantor--

46
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:01,170
someone to sign for the loan for you.

47
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:03,230
Why is that necessary?

48
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:04,580
Since you don't have enough income,

49
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:06,690
and you don't already own any property,

50
00:02:06,690 --> 00:02:08,020
the bank needs to be sure

51
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:09,920
you can pay the mortgage every month.

52
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:11,910
A guarantor is responsible for the loan

53
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:14,210
if you can't make the payments.

54
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:21,080
I see. Well, the idea of buying a house is exciting.

55
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:24,870
Thank you, Mr. Riley. We'll read this over carefully.

56
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:25,930
Thank you.

57
00:02:25,930 --> 00:02:27,000
Good-bye. Thanks.

58
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,610
Good-bye. And hope to see you soon.

59
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:31,280
I hope so, too.

60
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,540
Take care.

61
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:52,540
Good-bye.

62
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,440
It all sounded so easy

63
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:57,670
until they mentioned needing collateral or a guarantor.

64
00:02:57,670 --> 00:03:00,690
We have no collateral.

65
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:02,050
And I don't think it's a good idea

66
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:05,250
to ask Dad to sign as a guarantor.

67
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:06,820
I don't feel right about it.

68
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:22,160
I understand your feelings about it, Richard.

69
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:30,060
We can get a loan from the bank

70
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:31,410
[03:25.43]if we can put up some collateral.

71
00:03:31,410 --> 00:03:33,650
And we don't own anything to use as collateral.

72
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:39,270
Or someone can sign with us as a guarantor.

73
00:03:39,270 --> 00:03:41,180
Why don't you speak to Dad?

74
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:46,330
No. If we buy a house, I want to be able to handle it alone.

75
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:49,520
Everybody needs help sometimes, Richard.

76
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,690
I understand Richard's feelings about it, Ellen.

77
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:54,530
In two or three months, I'll have an advance on my book

78
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:57,570
and be able to put more money down.

79
00:03:57,570 --> 00:04:00,860
What about the house in Mount Kisco?

80
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,920
Somebody else'll buy it by then.

81
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,790
Then there'll be other houses, Marilyn.

82
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:10,390
Richard has a point. You're just beginning to look. Richard

83
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:11,450
We're in no great rush. It's true.

84
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:13,630
This has been a great learning experience for us, Marilyn.

85
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:15,720
Talking to the real-estate agent.

86
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:18,070
Looking at the houses.

87
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:21,890
Talking to the loan officer at the bank.

88
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:24,020
It has been a learning experience. That's true.

89
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:26,740
I think you're doing the right thing. Taking your time.

90
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:30,180
Looking around. Especially with a purchase of this kind.

91
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:33,740
You're talking about a lot of money.

92
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:37,210
We'll call Mrs. Martinelli and tell her to keep looking for us.

93
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:42,200
And I'll call Mr. Riley at the bank

94
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:42,880
and tell him we'll see him in a couple of months.

95
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,220
And if you ever need Dad or me to help you ...

96
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:46,300
We know.

97
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,480
You know we'll be there for you.

98
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:51,480
It's a Stewart tradition. We're a family.
